        {
            "heading": "Afro-Syncretic",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Rastafarianism: The primary religion of the Carribbean empire, based on the teachings of Marcus Garvey."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Voodoo: Vodouists worship a creator god, Bondye, and pray to his servants, the Loa, who act as intermediaries."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Santería: Translates roughly to \"devotion of the saints\", they worship three aspects of one god, with the saints acting as intermediaries."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Candomblé: The religion of the Brazilian invaders, a belief that focuses on worship through dance rituals."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Old World Cultists",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Americanism: This religion believes that a group known as the founding fathers were gods."
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "(Hamiltonian): Americanist heresy that believes that the founding fathers had implied powers not stated in their holy texts.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "(Jeffersonian): Americanist heresy that believes the common people and soldier of Ancient America should be revered in addition to the Founding Fathers.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "(Libertarian): Americanist heresy that believes in superiority of Lady Liberty in the Americanist pantheon.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Atomicists: This religion believes in a godlike power known as the Atom."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Consumerism: The followers of this religion believe that the Almighty Dollar caused The Event because Americans did not conduct the ritual known as the shopping enough."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Cult of Saints",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Sagrado Corazon: A religion in Mexico that is derived from Catholicism mixed with a pantheon of several quasi-deities from ancient Mexican folklore ."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Gracia Divina: A religion in Colombia that is derived from Catholicism mixed with a pantheon of local mythological figures, popular venerations of the Saints, and Bolivar deified as El Libertador."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Christians",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Evangelical: An alliance of Protestant churches from multiple denominations which form a single religion. It is centered in Holy Columbian Confederacy, and its power is heavily dependent on the authority of the Holy Columbian Emperor. Should the Emperor fail to deal with the coming Evangelical reformation properly, his authority, and that of the Evangelical Church Council, may be seriously damaged, reducing moral authority and beginning an event chain spreading heresy throughout the Evangelical world."
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "(Charismatic): Christian faith that believes God and the Holy Spirit speaks through miracles. It can be found throughout the Appalachians.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "(Antinomian): Christian faith that believes one can reach salvation based on faith alone and that one does not need to follow Mosaic law.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Anglican: The remnants of the Anglican Church of Canada, led by the Archbishop of Canterbury, New Brunswick. They can be found throughout Ontario and the Canadian Maritimes."
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "(United Church): The remnants of the United Church of Canada, the Anglican Church's chief rival. After suppression by the Anglicans, it can now only be found in Toronto and the Duchy of Thunder.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Catholic : A Catholic resurgence centered in the American Midwest, with a new Papacy in St. Louis. Unlike Ursuline Catholicism, it has undergone significant syncretization with the original Protestant denominations of the region."
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "(Sedevacantist): A Catholic heresy that refuses recognize the Pope in St.Louis and awaits the news of the existence or non-existence of the Roman Pope-Beyond-the-Sea.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "(Neo-Gnostic): A syncretic faith consisting of a mixture of Christian and Cetic teachings. It is considered a Catholic heresy due to its focus on the Christian part of its teachings. Its followers can be found throughout the Rocky Mountains, especially around the holy city of Denver.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "(Nestorian): Representing the remnants of the Chaldean Catholic Church, this group fell out of communion with the Pope in St. Louis and instead recognize the primacy of the Patriarch of the East in Chicago.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Ursuline: A group consisting of Christians who submit to the Abbess-General in Quebec and a female priesthood. They were Catholics in the distant past but now refuse to recognize the Pope in St.Louis."
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "(Angeline): An Ursuline heresy that believes in clerical cohabitation with the secular world and rejects cloistered monastic life.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Falling Star: A Christian religion championed by the Miskito people of Central America in the aftermath of the Event. Its theology is heavily influenced by the Moravian Church."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Anabaptist: A branch of Christianity which includes the Amish, Hutterites, and Mennonites. These groups banded together to survive in the post-Event world and now dominate upstate New York and central Pennsylvania."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Apostolic: A formerly Catholic Church that split from Rome before the Event. It is now the form of Christianity followed by the Brazilian emperors, and has several different branches."
                }
            ]
        },
